<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Armavir (ancient city)</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Argishtihinili</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Armavir was an ancient city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-ararat">Ararat</a> plain of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>, near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aras-river">Araxes</a> river. It grew on the site of the Urartian fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argishtihinili">Argishtihinili</a>, founded in the 8th century BCE, and became the capital of the Orontid kings of Armenia before they moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yervandashat">Yervandashat</a>. Greek inscriptions of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hellenistic-period">Hellenistic period</a> have been found there, and it gave its name to the modern Armenian province and town of Armavir.</p></div>
